From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cfgmgr32, sechost, user32: configuration manager notifications, service device events

- CM_Register_Notification returned CR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED and
  CM_Unregister_Notification was not exported (Firefox and other programs
  watch for devices with them). Over the device notifications sechost has
  from Wine's plug and play service:
  - an interface class, or all of them: DEVICEINTERFACEARRIVAL and
    DEVICEINTERFACEREMOVAL with the class and the interface's path;
  - a handle: the query-remove, remove and custom events (a custom event's
    GUID, name offset and data);
  - a device instance, or all of them: DEVICEINSTANCEENUMERATED and
    DEVICEINSTANCESTARTED when the first interface of the device arrives,
    DEVICEINSTANCEREMOVED when its interfaces have gone or it is no longer
    present (Wine's PnP manager reports interfaces, not device nodes).
  The filter is checked (size, flags, type, an instance or a handle). After
  CM_Unregister_Notification returns no callback runs, unless it was called
  from the callback itself, which does not hang.
- sechost: the first registration in a process waited for nothing, so an
  interface that arrived right after it was lost; it now returns once the
  process listens to the plug and play service.
- RegisterDeviceNotification with DEVICE_NOTIFY_SERVICE_HANDLE registered a
  callback that only printed a FIXME: the service's HandlerEx now gets
  SERVICE_CONTROL_DEVICEEVENT with the event and its data. A
  DBT_DEVTYP_HANDLE filter (a FIXME, though it worked) is checked for a
  handle.

Gate: test/cmnotify-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/cmnotify-probe.c, with a
plug and play client widl makes from test/cmnotify-plugplay.idl).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_CM_NOTIFY (cfgmgr32/main.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_SERVICE_DEVEVENT, SG_MUTANT_NO_LISTEN_WAIT
(sechost/service.c).
